# Testing

Run `./scripts/test.sh` from the repo root. That configures the Debug build and runs CTest (GoogleTest).

- Every new alert rule needs tests for the warning band, the critical band, and the exact threshold that must stay quiet. Critical suppresses warning on the same rule; test that only one alert comes back.
- Compare against the constants in `include/heliospan/rules.hpp`. Do not lock tests to a copied literal that will drift from the constant.
- HTTP tests live in `tests/test_api.cpp`. They start the server with the sampler paused. Tick the store explicitly when a test needs another reading.
- Simulator band tests should run many ticks and assert ranges, not a single float.
- Inject readings into `evaluate_readings` for rule tests. Do not sleep on the 2-second loop.
